  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nThe current mechanism of maxlength attribute is to enforce character limit while typing, which can be problematic for UX and accessibility reasons.\n\nIt simply does not allow user to add more characters than the defined value of maxlength, nor one can paste text without it being auto-cropped to the maxlength's value.\n\nI usually end up suggesting developers to not use it entirely and instead, write custom validation and error handling for the input.\n\n\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nCustom code using JavaScript or server-side validation.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nI imagine a new attribute could be introduced with soft enforcement like HTML input type email, by letting the user type however amount they want and only show a hint popover about the limit.\n\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
